This seventh visual novel from Zeiva Inc feature a gender-neutral protagonist Olea who had suddenly quit his/her job and decided to leave town and take a bus or walk towards a remote island village of Calcari Village which had been isolated for many years after a devastating earthquake and mudslide which caused many of its former inhabitants to leave the village and an ancient olive tree to wither and lose its leaves and flowers. As Olea settles into the village, Olea will meet Flori and Llima, two young adult girls who share their souls and visit the olive tree regularly in order to stay alive, a few minor supporting characters and 3 child spirits who will visit Olea in his/her sleep each night over 3 chapters(includes characters from Zeiva Inc's earlier visual novel
).
Although there are no Steam achievements to obtain in this game and the Steam take screenshot button feature doesn't work, the game has a memory fragment counter that will track and record each memory fragment that is awarded with each different decision Olea(the player) makes and each different ending reached throughout in different playthroughs and there is a guide available at Zeiva Inc's website that will help players get all memory fragments and reach all 6 possible endings in the game. The game has beautiful artwork, great opening movie, theme song and soundtracks. Recommended when game with original ending theme DLC are at discount or in bundle offer as it takes less than 10 hours to read through all 6 endings and bonus content.

A pretty fun game with nice mechanics;
100% Orange juice is a game for those who are looking to "run" from highly competitive games and get themselves into a new atmosphere to pass time. The game is very fun and has some very interesting mechanics, it's very luck-based though, and literally everything can happens during a match, I was able to keep a♥♥♥♥♥♥score during the entire game and comeback at the last minutes of the game and win the match anyways.
It worth the buy, can be frustating sometimes, but mostly of the time is fun.

